  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  Presence stub for com.google.android.apps.maps (Google Maps). Android Auto
  refuses to start without a package by this name installed. This package
  satisfies that check and nothing else: it holds no permissions, declares no
  components, and contains no code.

  Deliberately absent, and why:

    * No <intent-filter> for geo:, google.navigation:, http(s)://maps.google.*
      or android.intent.action.VIEW on map URIs. Declaring them would put this
      package in the disambiguation dialog for every map link on the device,
      and a user who picks it, or who has previously set "always", gets
      nothing. /e/OS ships Magic Earth (and, from 2026, Murena Maps); those
      should keep handling map intents.

    * No car-app or media service. Android Auto discovers navigation providers
      through CarAppService / androidx.car.app metadata. A stub that advertised
      one would appear on the car screen as a dead tile.

  Consequence, stated plainly: with this stub installed there is no Google Maps
  on the phone and therefore no Google Maps on the car screen. Navigation on
  the head unit has to come from another Android-Auto-capable app. See
  docs/09-android-auto-on-eos.md for which ones actually appear and why most
  do not.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.google.android.apps.maps"
    android:versionCode="1"
    android:versionName="0.1.0-openaap-stub">

    <uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion="33" android:targetSdkVersion="35" />

    <application
        android:label="Maps (Android Auto compatibility stub)"
        android:hasCode="false"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:forceQueryable="true" />

</manifest>
